## 2. Message Format

```text
24 3c | LL LL | 18 12 | SS | 01 | CC | D0 D1 D2 | RR RR
 ^magic  ^len.    ^fixed  ^cnt. ^app  ^command^data   ^CRC (little-endian)

```

| Byte | Meaning | Status |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **`24 3c`** | Start of message (Magic Header) | ✅ |
| **`LL LL`** | Payload length (little-endian). For the commands below it's `08 00` | ✅ |
| **`18 12`** | Fixed value in commands | ✅ |
| **`SS`** | Counter: +1 per message. The gimbal ignores duplicates | 🟡 |
| **`01`** | "Message from app to gimbal" (replies use `10`) | ✅ |
| **`CC`** | Command / axis number | ✅ |
| **`D0 D1 D2`** | Data. For movements: `10` + 16-bit little-endian value | ✅ |
| **`RR RR`** | CRC16 (little-endian) | ✅ |

### CRC

* **Algorithm:** CRC16 XMODEM (Polynomial `0x1021`, Initial value `0`, no reflection, XOR out `0`).
* **Calculation:** Computed **only** over the payload (from `18 12` to the last data byte).
* Verified on 5 real messages (table below).

```javascript
// JavaScript
function crc16(bytes) {
  let c = 0;
  for (const b of bytes) {
    c ^= b << 8;
    for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
      c = (c & 0x8000) ? ((c << 1) ^ 0x1021) & 0xFFFF : (c << 1) & 0xFFFF;
    }
  }
  return c;
}

```

```python
# Python
def crc16(data, crc=0):
    for b in data:
        crc ^= b << 8
        for _ in range(8):
            crc = ((crc << 1) ^ 0x1021) & 0xFFFF if crc & 0x8000 else (crc << 1) & 0xFFFF
    return crc

```

