## 3. Movements

| Command (`CC`) | Axis | Status |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **`01`** | Tilt (up / down) | ✅ (used for "pan up slow") |
| **`02`** | Pan (left / right) | 🟡 |
| **`03`** | Roll | 🟡 |

* **Value range:** `0` to `4095` ✅
* **`2048`:** Neutral / stopped 🟡 (Inferred: `3796` and `300` are `2048` ± `1748`)
* **`3796` and `300`:** Slow movement in two opposite directions 🟡

### ⚠️ Important Movement Note

The gimbal **only moves while messages keep arriving**. A single message moves the motors very little and then stops immediately.

* **Continuous Loop:** Repeat the current axis state every `~70 ms`.
* **Stopping:** To stop movement, send `2048` on all axes (sending it a few times in sequence is recommended).

